### 8.2 Accuracy versus coverage and abstention (descriptive, confidence ranking)

{{@matched_coverage}}

![Accuracy versus coverage](docs/figures/ml_coverage_accuracy.png)

The v1 shipped band answers {{v:v1_cov}} of windows at {{v:v1_acc_band}} accuracy and alerts {{v:v1_alert_band}} of all hypoxic windows; the v2 chain with its pulse-lock gate answers {{v:v2_cov}} at {{v:v2_acc_band}} and alerts {{v:v2_alert_band}}. Abstention is not detection: unanswered hypoxic windows are missed.

### 8.3 Calibration and conformal 3-state output

The nested conformal result below supersedes the descriptive ranking above where the two differ: it fixes the cutoffs from other people only.

{{@conformal_full}}

![Conformal output](docs/figures/ml_conformal.png)

**Reading.** The hybrid does not beat v1 at matched coverage ({{cm:final/v1/conformal_mondrian|d}} points at v1's coverage, {{cm:final/v2/conformal_mondrian|d}} at v2's; both intervals contain zero). The same conformal step on the v1 chain reads {{cm:chain_v1/v1/conformal_mondrian:acc|pct}} at v1's coverage and {{cm:chain_v1/v2/conformal_mondrian:acc|pct}} at v2's: the loss comes from the hybrid score, not from the conformal step. At alpha = 0.10 the hybrid alerts {{cf:final/0.1:alert_share_all|pct}} of all hypoxic windows and calls {{cf:final/0.1:confident_miss|pct}} of them Normal (target 10%). Set coverage holds approximately pooled and fails per person: person 1 has {{cpp:final/0.1/hof_100001:confident_miss|pct}} of its hypoxic windows called Normal. The thresholds shipped in the app (`app/data/conformal.json`) are fit on all six people and are therefore in-sample on the replay demo.

### 8.4 P2: heart rate

{{@p2_main}}

![HR Bland-Altman and error by dataset](docs/figures/ml_hr_blandaltman.png)

Rule selection on the Hoffman inner folds (6 people disjoint from every P2 test person): `spec` {{hr:spec:within5_full}}, `agree` {{hr:agree:within5_full}}, `guard` {{hr:guard:within5_full}}, `gate` {{hr:gate:within5_full}}, `cnn` {{hr:cnn:within5_full}}. The pre-registered "win" ({{hpd:all/v2_spectral_acf__forced|d}}) rests on a rule chosen after the pooled table had been seen (Amendment 3); on Hoffman alone the spectral estimator is best.

{{@hrvote_full}}

### 8.5 P3: absolute SpO2 (not headlined)

{{@p3_main}}

MTHS is normoxic, so nothing beats the train-mean predictor, including the CNN ({{cp:P3/-1/train_mean|d}}). The OpenOximetry arterial-blood-gas analysis is the SpO2 test that matters:

{{@openox_full}}

![OpenOximetry skin tone](docs/figures/ml_openox_skin.png)

The CNN ties the textbook ratio-of-ratios on the contact sensor ({{oxp:lag_star/R/ror_textbook|d}} MAE points) and beats the training mean ({{oxp:lag_star/R/train_mean|d}}); the dark-minus-light MAE gap by ITA tertile is {{oxg:ita/R/mae|d}} ({{oxg:ita/R/mae|n}} people), a tie, and not estimable by Monk group with 2 dark-skinned held-out people. No claim about phone SpO2 follows, and no SpO2 number is shown to users.

### 8.6 Ablations and levers

{{@ablation}}

Variants: `no_ssl` = stage B from scratch, no SSL; `no_pretrain` = neither (exploratory); `no_physics` = ratio-of-ratios channels, beat mask and their side features zeroed (baseline-relative DC stays); `no_openox` = SSL without OpenOximetry, no stage B; `no_aug`; `no_basecond` = baseline-relative inputs and embedding subtraction removed; `hr_only` = HR and quality heads only; `win20` = two consecutive 10 s feature windows; `adv` = gradient-reversal domain head. Single-seed rows compare with the full seed-0 row of the same protocol.

